# Design rules

This app is a financial ledger with a vibrant neon visual system. Numbers are still the content; colour and motion make them pop.

- Never invent colours, sizes, or spacing. Use only the tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css`. If a value you need does not exist, stop and ask.
- Type sizes are limited to: 12, 14, 16, 20, 28, 44, 64. Nothing between.
- Spacing uses only: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48. Nothing between.
- Every currency figure uses `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Prefer right-aligned in tables/lists; hero balances may be left-aligned.
- Cards use generous radius (`--r-xl` / 20px+). Light mode: soft drop shadow (no border). Dark mode: lifted surface (no heavy shadow). Do not combine border + shadow.
- Accents are neon: electric cyan, hot pink, vibrant yellow, bright green. Primary CTA uses `--flow` with `--on-accent` text.
- Light mode header sections may use `--header-gradient` (magenta → orange). Dark mode ground is `#1A1A2E`.
- Category emoji icons (`categoryEmoji`) are allowed as playful affordances; always pair with a text label.
- Minimum touch target 44px. Minimum input font-size 16px.
- Phone is the primary target. Design the 380px view first, then widen.
- Theme is user-controlled via `ThemeProvider` / `ThemeToggle` (`data-theme="light|dark"`).

Before writing any component, read `.cursor/rules/020-visual-system.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/021-mobile-ux.mdc`.

Do not add UI that is not in the spec. Ask first.
